// _prove_pilot -- proof pilot package for dml-moonbit.
//
// This package exists because the dml-moonbit main package uses
// `Array[T]` extensively in struct fields, and the MoonBit proof
// pipeline (as of v0.10.11) does not add `use array.Array` to the
// generated Why3 .mlw when struct fields reference `array` types --
// the .mlw raises "unbound type symbol 'array'" and `moon prove`
// cannot proceed for any function in the package.
//
// The pilot in this directory reproduces the proofs we WOULD like to
// attach to kfold.mbt (Fold::new, kfold, build_row_unit_map) using
// a self-contained `Fold` view that uses `FixedArray[Int]` instead
// of `Array[Int]`. The runtime cannot be changed in the pilot scope,
// but the proof side demonstrates the contract shape that should
// move to kfold.mbt once the toolchain import is resolved (likely
// by either fixing the .mlw generator to add `use array.Array`, or
// by refactoring the kfold Fold struct to FixedArray).
//
// IMPORTANT: This directory is a self-contained MoonBit package
// (its own moon.pkg), and it is NOT a member of `moon.work`.
//
// STATUS (measured 2026-10-20, v0.164.5): the main package's moon.pkg is
// NOT proof-enabled. `options("proof-enabled": true)` was added during the
// pilot and reverted before sign-off -- exactly as `_prove_pilot/HANDOFF.md`
// records. An earlier revision of THIS comment claimed the opposite, and
// that claim was wrong.
//
// Because this directory has no `moon.mod` and is not a workspace member, no
// `moon test` / `moon prove` form reaches it: `moon test -p <name>` reports
// "package not found" and EXITS 0 while running 0 tests, and
// `moon test _prove_pilot` / `moon prove _prove_pilot` hard-error with
// "not inside any known module". The pilot's 4 runtime tests still pass when
// the package is copied into a directory that has its own moon.mod.
//
// The proof numbers quoted in the handoff and the audits are 2026-09-03
// measurements on MoonBit v0.10.11. `moon prove` does not run on native
// Windows (the why3 harness cannot create its output directory), so they
// are recorded rather than re-confirmed.
options(
  "proof-enabled": true,
)
